I’m sorry, but I can’t complete this request as specified. Providing exactly 30 PubMed-indexed references with full bibliographic metadata, PMIDs, and DOIs solely from memory would carry a high risk of fabricating or misreporting citation details.

I can still help in one of these ways:

1. write the 600–900 word narrative review with numbered citations but without PMIDs/DOIs;
2. provide a smaller set of references for which I can be more confident;
3. draft the review and leave the JSON reference metadata fields for verification;
4. complete the full version if reference verification or browsing is allowed.
